2:T13f5,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"BlogPosting","@id":"https://www.melius.com/blog/best-ai-creative-canvases-image-generation#article","headline":"Best AI creative canvases for image generation","description":"Five AI creative canvases compared on who builds the graph, which models you can reach, whether workflows are reusable, and how they price collaboration.","url":"https://www.melius.com/blog/best-ai-creative-canvases-image-generation","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.melius.com/blog/best-ai-creative-canvases-image-generation"},"datePublished":"2026-09-05","dateModified":"2026-09-05","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Melius Team","url":"https://www.melius.com"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://www.melius.com/#organization"},"isPartOf":{"@id":"https://www.melius.com/#website"},"inLanguage":"en-US","image":"https://www.melius.com/images/blog/best-ai-creative-canvases-image-generation/cover.webp","timeRequired":"PT12M","wordCount":2011,"articleSection":"Comparisons","keywords":"Comparisons"},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Blog","item":"https://www.melius.com/blog"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Best AI creative canvases for image generation","item":"https://www.melius.com/blog/best-ai-creative-canvases-image-generation"}]},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is an AI creative canvas?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It's a workspace where creative work is built as a graph rather than typed into a single prompt box: each prompt, image, video or edit is a node, and edges pass one node's output into the next. That structure means a multi-step pipeline lives visually in one place, and you can change an early step and re-run everything after it instead of starting again."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a node-based AI canvas?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A node-based canvas represents each creative step as a node you connect to others, so the whole pipeline is visible and editable. The advantage over a chat interface is that the process is kept, not lost: you can rewire a step, branch to compare two directions, or reuse a working graph as a template for the next job."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I have to learn node graphs to use one?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not on all of them. Krea, Flora, Figma Weave and ComfyUI all expect you to build the graph yourself, with ComfyUI asking the most. On Melius an agent builds and runs the graph from a plain-language description and leaves it there for you to inspect, so the node interface is available, not required."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is ComfyUI still worth learning in 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, if you want total control and are willing to maintain it. Its flexibility and its price are hard to argue with, and the community ecosystem around it is deep. The reason most creatives don't is the time cost: you become responsible for models, dependencies and hardware, and none of that is the creative work."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which AI canvas gives access to the most models?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"ComfyUI, in absolute terms, because you can install anything, including models no commercial platform hosts. Among hosted tools, the ones spanning image, video and audio across several providers on one subscription give the widest practical reach, and Melius keeps a live registry of what it currently supports. Model libraries change monthly, so check the current list instead of trusting a comparison post."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does an AI creative canvas cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"ComfyUI is free if you self-host. Among the paid tools, free plans exist across the board but are small, and the number that matters more than the headline price is how seats are charged: Flora prices per seat, Figma Weave's Team plan per user, and Melius includes up to 8 seats on self-serve plans and unlimited seats on Enterprise. Check each pricing page, because these change often."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can several people work on the same canvas?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"On some of them, and it's worth checking what it costs. Real multiplayer means a designer, a copywriter and a reviewer can all be in the same document while it's being built, which is the main argument for a canvas over individual tools. ComfyUI has effectively none, and the commercial tools differ mainly in whether collaboration is priced per head."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I own what I make on a creative canvas?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Usually, but confirm it per tool. On Melius you own what you create and can use it commercially, subject to the underlying model providers' terms, and Melius does not use your work to train AI models. Figma Weave includes a commercial license even on its free plan. Self-hosted ComfyUI leaves the question to the licences of whichever models you install."}}]}]}7:X
