18:["$","p","b2907",{"children":["Four criteria, and the first is the one that decides whether the tool gets used after week two."]}]
19:["$","h3","b2909",{"children":["Whether you have to learn it"]}]
1a:["$","p","b2911",{"children":["Node graphs are a real interface with real concepts, and most creatives have no interest in acquiring them. The question is whether the tool expects you to wire nodes yourself, or whether something else does that from a plain description while leaving the graph there for you to inspect. Both are valid; they suit different people."]}]
1b:["$","h3","b2913",{"children":["Which models you can reach"]}]
1c:["$","p","b2915",{"children":["The point of a canvas is combining steps, and steps are better when each can use the best model for its job. Material and fabric, legible type, faces, motion: these are won by different models, and a canvas limited to one family forces a compromise at every step. Check how the library is kept current, too, because this field moves monthly."]}]
1d:["$","h3","b2917",{"children":["Whether the graph is reusable"]}]
1e:["$","p","b2919",{"children":["Building a working pipeline is an investment, and it only pays back if you can point it at new inputs next week. Look for templates, saved workflows, or an equivalent, and check whether a saved graph accepts fresh inputs or has to be edited in place each time."]}]
1f:["$","h3","b2921",{"children":["Whether other people can work on it"]}]
20:["$","p","b2923",{"children":["Creative work is reviewed, and review that happens on the canvas beats review that happens in a thread of exported screenshots. Multiplayer matters, and so does what it costs: a tool priced per seat quietly discourages the collaboration it advertises."]}]
21:["$","h2","b2925",{"id":"the-five-compared","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["The five compared"]}]
22:["$","div","b2926",{"role":"region","aria-label":"Comparison table, scroll horizontally to see all columns","tabIndex":0,"data-lenis-prevent":true,"className":"my-10 max-w-full overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-black/10 bg-white shadow-[0_1px_2px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-orange","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full min-w-[640px] border-collapse text-left","children":["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","b2927",{"className":"bg-black/[0.04]","children":[["$","td","b29270",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b2930",{"children":[["$","strong","b2929",{"children":["Tool"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b29271",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b2933",{"children":[["$","strong","b2932",{"children":["Who builds the graph"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b29272",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b2936",{"children":[["$","strong","b2935",{"children":["Ease of use"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b29273",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b2939",{"children":[["$","strong","b2938",{"children":["Model choice"]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b2940",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b29400",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2943",{"children":["Melius"]}]]}],["$","td","b29401",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2946",{"children":["An agent, from a plain-language brief"]}]]}],["$","td","b29402",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2949",{"children":["5/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b29403",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2952",{"children":["Image, video and audio across many providers"]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b2953",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b29530",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2956",{"children":["Krea"]}]]}],["$","td","b29531",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2959",{"children":["You do, on a suite rather than a node graph"]}]]}],["$","td","b29532",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2962",{"children":["4/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b29533",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2965",{"children":["Wide, with its own real-time and upscale models"]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b2966",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b29660",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2969",{"children":["Flora"]}]]}],["$","td","b29661",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2972",{"children":["You do, with Flows to structure it"]}]]}],["$","td","b29662",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2975",{"children":["3/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b29663",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2978",{"children":["Image, video and text"]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b2979",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b29790",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2982",{"children":["Figma Weave"]}]]}],["$","td","b29791",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2985",{"children":["You do, wiring nodes by hand"]}]]}],["$","td","b29792",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":"$L5e"}],"$L5f"]}],"$L60"]}]}]}]
23:["$","h2","b3006",{"id":"1-melius","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["1. Melius"]}]
24:["$","p","b3008",{"children":["Melius is the Agentic OS for creative work, and the first node-based canvas made for agents. You describe the work in plain language, Mel, the Melius agent, wires the graph, routes each node to the right model and runs it, and every prompt and step stays open for you to change. The canvas is there when you want it and ignorable when you don't, which is the whole design."]}]
25:["$","p","b3010",{"children":["It's also the only one here you can drive from outside the app. Slack, an application programming interface (API), a command-line interface (CLI), and Model Context Protocol (MCP) all act on the same canvas, so the work can start wherever you already are."]}]
26:["$","h3","b3012",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
27:["$","ul","b3014-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b3014",{"children":["An agent builds and runs the graph from a description, so the node interface is optional, not a prerequisite."]}],["$","li","b3016",{"children":["One subscription spanning image, video and audio models from several providers, with per-step routing."]}],["$","li","b3018",{"children":["Templates ship in the product, covering the common jobs, and a working graph can be reused as one."]}],["$","li","b3020",{"children":["Multiplayer with multiple people and multiple agents on one canvas at the same time, and up to 8 seats on self-serve plans and unlimited seats on Enterprise."]}],["$","li","b3022",{"children":["Search with AI on the Professional plan, so generations and uploads stay searchable instead of getting lost."]}],["$","li","b3024",{"children":["Nothing is a black box: change an early node and everything downstream re-runs."]}]]}]
28:["$","p","b3032",{"children":["The seat pricing is the underrated part. Every other tool on this list either charges per person or assumes one, and a canvas is a collaboration surface, so paying per head to let a stakeholder look at the work cuts against the reason you bought it. Self-serve plans include up to 8 seats for your team and reviewers, with unlimited seats on Enterprise. Plans start at $18 a month as of August 2026, current pricing is on the ",["$","$L61","b3027",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b3026","href":"/pricing","isNewTab":false},"children":["pricing page"]}],", and the current library of leading models is listed on the ",["$","$L61","b3030",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b3029","href":"/models","isNewTab":false},"children":["models page"]}],"."]}]
29:["$","p","b3034",{"children":["The catch: an agent is only as good as the brief. A vague description produces a vague graph, and you'll still want to look at the canvas when the output isn't what you meant."]}]
2a:["$","p","b3036",{"children":["Best for: creative teams who want the benefits of a node pipeline without anyone having to become a node person."]}]
2b:["$","h2","b3038",{"id":"2-krea","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["2. Krea"]}]
2c:["$","p","b3040",{"children":["Krea is a fast way to explore, and it gets there by not being a node graph. It's a creative suite with a canvas surface, built around real-time generation where the image updates as you move things, which is a genuinely different feel from prompt-and-wait."]}]
2d:["$","p","b3042",{"children":["The breadth is the other draw. Image, video, 3D, real-time, upscaling and its own fine-tuning all sit in one subscription, with a large model library and a very large style catalogue behind a deliberately spare interface."]}]
2e:["$","h3","b3044",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
2f:["$","ul","b3046-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b3046",{"children":["Real-time generation, which makes exploration feel like sketching rather than querying."]}],["$","li","b3048",{"children":["A wide model library plus its own models, including upscaling to very large output sizes."]}],["$","li","b3050",{"children":["Training your own style, so a look becomes reproducible without prompt archaeology."]}],["$","li","b3052",{"children":["A clean interface that hides most of the complexity, which suits solo work."]}],["$","li","b3054",{"children":["A daily free allowance of 100 compute units, enough to evaluate it properly."]}]]}]
30:["$","p","b3056",{"children":["Because it isn't node-based, multi-step pipelines are weaker here. There's no real equivalent of a saved graph you point at new inputs, so repeatable production work means repeating yourself. Collaboration is thin too: this is a tool built around one person exploring quickly."]}]
31:["$","p","b3058",{"children":["The catch: superb for exploration, structurally unsuited to a workflow you run every week."]}]
32:["$","p","b3060",{"children":["Best for: solo creatives and designers who want speed and range over repeatability."]}]
33:["$","h2","b3062",{"id":"3-flora","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["3. Flora"]}]
34:["$","p","b3064",{"children":["Flora is a genuine node canvas with a narrative bent. Its Flows feature structures a graph along a story arc, which makes it a natural fit for storyboarding, sequences and anything where the output is a series, not a single asset."]}]
35:["$","p","b3066",{"children":["Of the hand-wired canvases here it's the friendliest. The interface is designed for creatives, not engineers, and the concepts arrive gradually enough that a designer can get productive without a tutorial marathon."]}]
36:["$","h3","b3068",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
37:["$","ul","b3070-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b3070",{"children":["Flows structure a workflow along a narrative arc, which suits storyboards and sequences."]}],["$","li","b3072",{"children":["A node canvas designed for creatives, with a gentler learning curve than the engineering-first tools."]}],["$","li","b3074",{"children":["Image, video and text nodes in one graph."]}],["$","li","b3076",{"children":["Genuinely pleasant to use, which matters more than it sounds for adoption."]}],["$","li","b3078",{"children":["A free plan to try it, though a small one."]}]]}]
38:["$","p","b3083",{"children":["The free tier is the tightest on this list, capped at a small lifetime allowance instead of a monthly one, so evaluating it properly means paying. Pricing is per seat, which adds up quickly for a team, and you still build every graph yourself. There's a fuller side-by-side in our ",["$","$L61","b3081",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b3080","href":"/blog/flora-alternative","isNewTab":false},"children":["Flora alternative piece"]}]," if you're weighing the two directly."]}]
39:["$","p","b3085",{"children":["The catch: you're still the one wiring it, and the seat pricing punishes collaboration."]}]
3a:["$","p","b3087",{"children":["Best for: creatives working on sequences and narrative-shaped output who want a canvas that doesn't feel like software."]}]
3b:["$","h2","b3089",{"id":"4-figma-weave","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["4. Figma Weave"]}]
3c:["$","p","b3091",{"children":["Figma Weave is the node canvas with the strongest institutional backing. Formerly Weavy, it was acquired by Figma in October 2025, and it chains image, video, 3D and editing steps as nodes you connect and run."]}]
3d:["$","p","b3093",{"children":["Its real advantage is where it sits. If your team already works in Figma, having generation adjacent to design files removes an export step and a lot of context switching, and that convenience beats a better model most days."]}]
3e:["$","h3","b3095",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
3f:["$","ul","b3097-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b3097",{"children":["A proper node canvas for chaining generation and editing steps."]}],["$","li","b3099",{"children":["Full access to all its supported AI image models on every plan, including the free one."]}],["$","li","b3101",{"children":["A commercial license included on the free plan, which is unusually generous."]}],["$","li","b3103",{"children":["Figma's backing, which is the strongest signal here that the tool will still exist in three years."]}],["$","li","b3105",{"children":["Adjacency to design files for teams already standardised on Figma."]}]]}]
40:["$","p","b3110",{"children":["You wire everything by hand, and the free plan's 5 workflows and 150 monthly credits go quickly once you're doing real work. The Team plan is priced per user, so a canvas a whole team can open is the expensive configuration. Our ",["$","$L61","b3108",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b3107","href":"/blog/figma-weave-alternative","isNewTab":false},"children":["Figma Weave alternative piece"]}]," covers the comparison in more detail."]}]
41:["$","p","b3112",{"children":["The catch: excellent if you live in Figma, and a hand-built graph either way."]}]
42:["$","p","b3114",{"children":["Best for: design teams already standardised on Figma who want generation in the same neighbourhood."]}]
43:["$","h2","b3116",{"id":"5-comfyui","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["5. ComfyUI"]}]
44:["$","p","b3118",{"children":["ComfyUI is where this whole category started, and it's free. It's open source with well over a hundred thousand stars on GitHub, it runs on your own hardware, and it will run models no hosted tool exposes."]}]
45:["$","p","b3120",{"children":["For a technical artist who wants that level of control, it's still the right trade. Total control over every model, parameter and output, no per-generation billing, and no vendor deciding which models you're allowed to reach."]}]
46:["$","h3","b3122",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
47:["$","ul","b3124-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b3124",{"children":["Complete control over every model, parameter and step in the pipeline."]}],["$","li","b3126",{"children":["Free and open source, self-hosted on your own graphics processing unit (GPU), with no usage metering."]}],["$","li","b3128",{"children":["Any model you can install, including ones no commercial platform hosts."]}],["$","li","b3130",{"children":["An enormous ecosystem of community nodes and shared workflows."]}],["$","li","b3132",{"children":["Comfy Cloud for a hosted option if you'd rather not run the hardware."]}]]}]
48:["$","p","b3134",{"children":["The cost is time, and it's substantial. You manage models, dependencies and hardware, and the learning curve is the steepest here by a wide margin. Collaboration is barely there, and a graph that works on your machine is not automatically a graph that works on a colleague's. This is exactly the trade Melius is built to avoid: the canvas is the right infrastructure, and most creatives shouldn't have to learn it to benefit from it."]}]
49:["$","p","b3136",{"children":["The catch: unlimited capability in exchange for becoming the person who maintains it."]}]
4a:["$","p","b3138",{"children":["Best for: technical artists and engineers who want control and have the patience the tool demands."]}]
4b:["$","h2","b3140",{"id":"when-you-don-t-need-a-canvas-at-all","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["When you don't need a canvas at all"]}]
4c:["$","p","b3142",{"children":["A canvas is overhead, and for a decent share of creative work the overhead isn't worth it."]}]
4d:["$","p","b3144",{"children":["If your job is one image from one prompt, a single-model tool is faster and you should use one. If it's a finished, laid-out social post, a design tool with templates will get you there sooner. If it's a one-off you'll never repeat, the investment in building a graph has nothing to pay back. The canvas earns its keep at the point where a job has several steps and you'll run something like it again, which is when starting over each time becomes the expensive option."]}]
4e:["$","p","b3149",{"children":["The other honest limit is that a canvas doesn't improve the models. Every tool here draws on broadly the same frontier models, so a canvas won't make a weak generation good. What it changes is how much of your work survives: the process is kept, inspectable and re-runnable, instead of disappearing into a chat thread you can't reconstruct next month. Who assembles that graph is a separate question, covered in our comparison of ",["$","$L61","b3147",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b3146","href":"/blog/agentic-image-generation-tools-compared","isNewTab":false},"children":["agentic image generation tools"]}],"."]}]
4f:["$","h2","b3151",{"id":"frequently-asked-questions","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["Frequently asked questions"]}]
50:["$","div","b3152",{"className":"faq-list my-10 flex flex-col divide-y divide-black/10 border-y border-black/10","children":[["$","details","0",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["What is an AI creative canvas?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"It's a workspace where creative work is built as a graph rather than typed into a single prompt box: each prompt, image, video or edit is a node, and edges pass one node's output into the next. That structure means a multi-step pipeline lives visually in one place, and you can change an early step and re-run everything after it instead of starting again."}]]}],["$","details","1",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["What is a node-based AI canvas?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"A node-based canvas represents each creative step as a node you connect to others, so the whole pipeline is visible and editable. The advantage over a chat interface is that the process is kept, not lost: you can rewire a step, branch to compare two directions, or reuse a working graph as a template for the next job."}]]}],["$","details","2",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Do I have to learn node graphs to use one?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Not on all of them. Krea, Flora, Figma Weave and ComfyUI all expect you to build the graph yourself, with ComfyUI asking the most. On Melius an agent builds and runs the graph from a plain-language description and leaves it there for you to inspect, so the node interface is available, not required."}]]}],["$","details","3",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Is ComfyUI still worth learning in 2026?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],"$L62"]}],"$L63","$L64","$L65","$L66"]}]
51:["$","p","b3157",{"children":["Describe the pipeline you want in plain language and let an agent wire the graph, then open the canvas only if you want to change how it works. ",["$","$L61","b3155",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b3154","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true},"children":["Open Melius"]}],"."]}]
52:["$","section","related",{"className":"relative w-full pb-section bg-gray-background","children":[["$","$L11",null,{"color":"gray"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"relative z-10 mx-auto w-full max-w-300 px-5 lg:px-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"t-h-2 mb-12 text-center text-balance text-gray-dark-1","children":"Related Articles"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto grid w-full max-w-max grid-cols-1 gap-11 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3","children":[["$","$L67","post-turn-picture-into-professional-headshot-tools-ranked",{"post":{"_key":"post-turn-picture-into-professional-headshot-tools-ranked","slug":"turn-picture-into-professional-headshot-tools-ranked","category":"comparisons","title":"Tools to turn a picture into a professional headshot, ranked","isoDate":"2026-09-03","date":"September 3, 2026","readTime":"10 Min Read","excerpt":"Turn a picture into a professional headshot with five tools ranked on likeness, team consistency, and the work required to reuse each portrait.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/turn-picture-into-professional-headshot-tools-ranked/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Alex Chen, Member of Technical Staff"}],"faq":[{"question":"What is the best tool to turn a picture into a professional headshot?","answer":"For a matching set across a team, Melius is the strongest fit because the treatment can be written down once and reapplied to every portrait. If one person's headshots are the whole requirement, HeadshotPro and Aragon are faster, more focused options. Krea's LoRA training is useful when you need a model to learn one person's face rather than work from a reference."},{"question":"Why do AI headshots look fake?","answer":"Usually the problem is over-processing rather than a bad likeness. Skin gets smoothed until it looks plastic and eyes get made too even. Reduce enhancement before changing tools, and judge results at the size people will actually see them."},{"question":"How do I keep headshots consistent across a whole team?","answer":"Define the specification once in a central place and apply it to every portrait. Whether it lives in an administrator setting or a written treatment on a canvas matters less than having one source of truth. Letting each person choose their own look is what produces a mismatched team page."},{"question":"How many photos do I need for an AI headshot?","answer":"It depends on the tool. Melius can work from one good reference portrait, while dedicated generators usually ask for several selfies. More angles help a trained model learn a face, but source quality sets the ceiling: use a sharp, evenly lit, front-facing photo whenever possible."},{"question":"Can I use an AI headshot on LinkedIn or a company site?","answer":"Generally yes, but terms differ by tool and should be checked before a company-wide rollout. On Melius, you own what you create and can use it commercially, subject to the underlying model providers' terms. Decide as a team whether you want to disclose AI use, since norms are still forming."},{"question":"Is a creative platform overkill for headshots?","answer":"For one headshot, yes: a dedicated generator is usually the quickest route. It stops being overkill when portraits must follow a brand specification, survive the next hire, or appear in a deck, site bio, and campaign at different crops."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"how-do-you-turn-a-picture-into-a-professional-headshot","title":"How to turn a picture into a headshot"},{"_key":"what-to-know-before-you-pick","title":"Before you pick"},{"_key":"what-separates-a-good-headshot-tool","title":"What separates them"},{"_key":"the-five-compared","title":"The five compared"},{"_key":"1-melius","title":"1. Melius"},{"_key":"2-headshotpro","title":"2. HeadshotPro"},{"_key":"3-aragon-ai","title":"3. Aragon AI"},{"_key":"4-betterpic","title":"4. BetterPic"},{"_key":"5-krea","title":"5. Krea"},{"_key":"where-this-is-heading","title":"Where this is heading"},{"_key":"build-the-portrait-into-the-wider-creative","title":"Use it in the wider workflow"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"FAQ"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2629","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2628","text":"How do you turn a picture into a professional headshot?","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"how-do-you-turn-a-picture-into-a-professional-headshot"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2631","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2630","text":"Feed a clean source portrait into a tool that can hold the face steady while it changes everything around it. Backdrop, wardrobe, lighting, and crop need to move while the person stays recognizably themselves.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2633","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2632","text":"Dedicated headshot generators are the right answer for many people. Give one several selfies and it returns a set of finished headshots without asking you to build a workflow. This ranking is for the job that outlasts the first purchase: portraits that match each other, survive the next hire, and get recut for the site, deck, and campaign where they end up.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2635","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2634","text":"What to know before you pick","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-to-know-before-you-pick"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2637","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2636","text":"Likeness and consistency are different problems, and few tools excel at both","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2639","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2638","text":"A per-person purchase is fine for one headshot and awkward for a company that keeps hiring","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2641","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2640","text":"Portraits punish over-processing harder than most subjects, so aggressive enhancement often works against you","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2643","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2642","text":"Check output resolution, aspect ratios, and commercial-use terms before you commit","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2645","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2644","text":"What separates a good headshot tool?","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-separates-a-good-headshot-tool"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2647","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2646","text":"Four criteria matter, and they are mostly in tension with one another.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2649","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2648","text":"It holds the face","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2651","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2650","text":"The person has to stay themselves. Identity drift makes an AI headshot unusable because colleagues notice it immediately, even when they cannot name what is wrong.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2653","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2652","text":"It resists over-processing","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2655","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2654","text":"The standard complaint about AI portraits is plastic-looking skin and overly even eyes. Tools that invent detail aggressively tend to overcook faces, so the most aggressive enhancement is not necessarily the best portrait treatment.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2657","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2656","text":"It repeats across people","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2659","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2658","text":"One good portrait is a demo. A team page needs the same backdrop, crop, and lighting for people who join at different times, so the treatment must live somewhere reusable outside an individual session.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2661","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2660","text":"It gives you the crops you actually ship","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2663","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2662","text":"A headshot lands in a profile square, site bio, deck, and slide template. A tool that returns one aspect ratio has handed you a cropping job.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2665","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2664","text":"The five compared","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"the-five-compared"},{"_type":"portableTable","_key":"b2666","rows":[{"_key":"b2667","cells":[{"_key":"b2668","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2670","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2669","text":"","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b2671","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2673","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2672","text":"Holds a face via","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b2674","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2676","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2675","text":"Repeats across a team","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b2677","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2679","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2678","text":"Portrait risk","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b2680","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2682","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2681","text":"Crops and resizing","marks":["strong"]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b2683","cells":[{"_key":"b2684","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2686","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2685","text":"Melius","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2687","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2689","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2688","text":"Reference portrait plus written treatment","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2690","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2692","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2691","text":"Treatment reused as text","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2693","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2695","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2694","text":"Model-choice dependent","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2696","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2698","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2697","text":"Magic Resize re-composes per ratio","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b2699","cells":[{"_key":"b2700","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2702","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2701","text":"HeadshotPro","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2703","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2705","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2704","text":"Several selfies per person","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2706","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2708","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2707","text":"Admin-set style","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2709","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2711","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2710","text":"Typical category risk","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2712","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2714","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2713","text":"Headshot-focused output","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b2715","cells":[{"_key":"b2716","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2718","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2717","text":"Aragon AI","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2719","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2721","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2720","text":"Several uploaded photos","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2722","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2724","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2723","text":"Team albums and approval","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2725","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2727","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2726","text":"Reviewers report plastic-looking skin","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2728","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2730","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2729","text":"Headshot-focused output","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b2731","cells":[{"_key":"b2732","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2734","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2733","text":"BetterPic","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2735","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2737","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2736","text":"Casual phone photos","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2738","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2740","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2739","text":"Seats and bulk credits","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2741","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2743","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2742","text":"Typical category risk","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2744","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2746","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2745","text":"Headshot-focused output","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b2747","cells":[{"_key":"b2748","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2750","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2749","text":"Krea","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2751","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2753","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2752","text":"LoRA trained on a specific face","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2754","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2756","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2755","text":"No shared team treatment","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2757","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2759","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2758","text":"Enhancement can invent detail","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2760","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2762","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2761","text":"Manual","marks":[]}]}]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2764","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2763","text":"1. Melius","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"1-melius"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2766","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2765","text":"Melius is the Agentic OS for creative work, a node-based creative canvas that AI agents operate with you. It leads here because a portrait can sit inside the rest of your creative: the same treatment produces the profile square, the site crop, the deck ratio, and a portrait that matches the campaign around it.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2768","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2767","text":"Picture to Headshot turns a photo into a professional headshot. Casual to Corporate turns a full-body shot into a corporate portrait, and Face Retouch smooths skin, clears blemishes, and evens tone while keeping the photo natural.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2770","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2769","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2772","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2771","text":"Starts with a headshot template that you can modify, so the treatment becomes yours","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2774","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2773","text":"Lets you choose the model best suited to holding skin tone and editorial lighting","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2776","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2775","text":"Uses Remove Background for a shared backdrop and Portrait Mode for a blurred-background look","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2778","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2777","text":"Uses Magic Resize to make profile, bio, and deck crops by re-composing rather than trimming","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2780","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2779","text":"Keeps review and approval on a multiplayer canvas with comment threads","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2782","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2781","text":"A canvas asks more of you on the first portrait than a single upload button does, so a single upload and generation task does not need all that a canvas can do. You own what you create and can use it commercially, subject to the underlying model providers' terms, and Melius does not use your work to train AI models.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2785","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2783","text":"Best for: ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2784","text":"brand and people teams standardizing portraits across a company, and anyone whose headshot must match the rest of what they publish.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2787","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2786","text":"2. HeadshotPro","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"2-headshotpro"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2789","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2788","text":"HeadshotPro is a strong dedicated option for a team. An administrator sets styling preferences and employees upload selfies against them, so the look is centralized without anyone running a canvas.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2791","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2790","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2793","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2792","text":"An administrator-set style that staff can self-serve into","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2795","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2794","text":"Team pricing and volume discounts designed for growing headcounts","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2797","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2796","text":"Enterprise controls including single sign-on and data-processing support","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2799","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2798","text":"A focused process that returns a set of headshot options quickly","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2801","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2800","text":"What you buy is headshots, and only headshots. If the portrait also has to appear in a deck template, a site bio at another crop, or a campaign that matches other creative, that work happens elsewhere.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2804","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2802","text":"Best for: ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2803","text":"a company-wide rollout where an administrator sets the look once and staff self-serve into it.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2806","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2805","text":"3. Aragon AI","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"3-aragon-ai"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2808","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2807","text":"Aragon is a polished individual product with a straightforward upload flow and paid turnaround tiers. It is designed to turn a small set of uploaded photos into a larger selection of professional headshots.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2810","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2809","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2812","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2811","text":"A small photo set in and a large selection of headshots out","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2814","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2813","text":"Turnaround options for people who need a result quickly","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2816","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2815","text":"A team offering with custom attire, backgrounds, administrators, and album approval","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2818","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2817","text":"Enterprise controls for larger organizations","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2820","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2819","text":"The recurring criticism worth knowing is realism: some users report skin that looks plastic. That is the failure mode that matters most on a face, so test output on your own photos before committing a team.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2823","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2821","text":"Best for: ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2822","text":"an individual who wants many options quickly and a clear upgrade path if a team later needs the same thing.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2825","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2824","text":"4. BetterPic","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"4-betterpic"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2827","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2826","text":"BetterPic is worth considering when headcount is large and cost per person matters. Its team offering is structured around seats and volume credits, while its individual plans return different volumes and style choices from casual phone photos.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2829","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2828","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2831","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2830","text":"Volume pricing intended for larger batches of people","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2833","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2832","text":"An entry route for testing output before committing broadly","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2835","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2834","text":"A guided casual-phone-photo input process","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2837","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2836","text":"A broad selection of finished headshots from one upload session","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2839","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2838","text":"Read the style counts carefully. A style can mean one background, clothing treatment, and color combination, so lower tiers may give volume inside one look rather than choices across several looks.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2842","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2840","text":"Best for: ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2841","text":"large headcounts where the per-person cost is the deciding number.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2844","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2843","text":"5. Krea","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"5-krea"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2846","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2845","text":"Krea is last because it takes the most work, and it is here because it is the route where you train the model yourself. Its Train workflow supports character LoRAs, where you upload a focused image set and create a custom model you can use beyond a fixed menu of headshot styles.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2848","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2847","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2850","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2849","text":"Custom LoRA training that learns one person's face from examples","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2852","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2851","text":"A focused training dataset that you can reuse when iterating on the same subject","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2854","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2853","text":"A trained character model that can remain private","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2856","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2855","text":"A flexible generation workflow rather than a fixed headshot-style menu","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2858","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2857","text":"The qualifier is everything after the face is right. Krea has no dedicated headshot template, no team-level treatment you define once and hand to many people, and no re-composing step for the crops a portrait actually ships in. Its enhancement can also invent detail, which is a liability on a face.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2861","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2859","text":"Best for: ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2860","text":"one person's likeness learned properly, when the portraits do not need to match anyone else's.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2863","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2862","text":"Where this is heading","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"where-this-is-heading"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2865","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2864","text":"Likeness is becoming a commodity. Holding one face across many generations used to be a research problem and is now a baseline expectation. The durable question is whose specification a portrait follows, whether it survives the next hire, and whether it matches the deck, site, and campaign where it appears.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2867","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2866","text":"That is an organizational problem wearing a technical costume. Buy for repeatability when the portrait has to work as a system; buy a specialist when one person's headshot is the whole job.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2869","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2868","text":"Build the portrait into the wider creative","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"build-the-portrait-into-the-wider-creative"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2877","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b2871","href":"/blog/best-ai-photo-background-editing-tools","isNewTab":false},{"_type":"link","_key":"b2874","href":"/blog/best-ai-tools-turn-images-into-painting","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2870","text":"A shared background is only one part of a portrait treatment. For the surrounding edit work, see ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2872","text":"the best AI photo background editing tools","marks":["b2871"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2873","text":". If the visual direction needs to become a reusable style rather than a fixed headshot template, see ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2875","text":"the best AI tools to turn images into a painting","marks":["b2874"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2876","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2882","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b2879","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2878","text":"If you need one headshot, use one of the specialists above. If you need a matching set that fits the rest of what you publish, start from the Picture to Headshot template in ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2880","text":"Melius","marks":["b2879"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2881","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2884","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2883","text":"Frequently asked questions","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"frequently-asked-questions"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b2885","items":"$52:props:children:1:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:post:faq"}]}}],"$L68","$L69"]}]]}]]}]
